                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Fines.fs",
                "line": 27,
                "quote": "List.sumBy (fun fine -> match fine.Waiver with Some w -> w.PaidBefore | None -> fine.Amount)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 13,
                "quote": "| Some waiver -> waiver.PaidBefore"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 28,
                "quote": "fine.Waiver |> Option.map (fun w -> w.PaidBefore) |> Option.defaultValue 0m"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The fact that a waived fine counts only for what was paid on it is written three times: Accounts.counted, the Fines.outstanding inline match, and the frozen sum in allocations. Fines.outstanding does not reuse the private counted. The fully-paid predicate in Views and Waivers (applied < fine.Amount) is also repeated. Today the copies agree, but they can drift. The borrow-block rule now has a single definition via Accounts.isBlocked.",
